.TH expr_area 3 2026-10-23 "Graph Drawer expr man-pages 1.0.13"
.SH NAME
expr_area_* \- memory allocator
.SH LIBRARY
Graph Drawer Expression Evaluator Library
.RI ( libexpr ,\~ \-lexpr )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BR #include\~"expr.h"
.P
.BI "int expr_area_init(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",void *" zone ",size_t " size ");"
.BI "int expr_area_init4(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",void *" zone ",size_t " size ",int " flag ");"
.BI "void expr_area_wipe(struct expr_area *restrict " area ");"
.BI "void expr_area_wipe_monotonic(struct expr_area *restrict " area ");"
.BI "void expr_area_reset_monotonic(struct expr_area *restrict " area ");"
.BI "int expr_area_resize(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",size_t " size ");"
.BI "void *expr_area_malloc(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",size_t " size ");"
.BI "void *expr_area_malloc3(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",size_t " size ",int " flag ");"
.BI "void expr_area_dealloc(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",void *" old ");"
.BI "void *expr_area_realloc(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",void *" old ",size_t " size ");"
.BI "void *expr_area_realloc4(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",void *" old ",size_t " size ",int " flag ");"
.BI "void *expr_area_calloc(struct expr_area *restrict " area ",size_t " size ");"
.BI "int expr_area_summary(const struct expr_area *restrict " area ",struct expr_areainfo *restrict " info ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR expr_area_init[4]()
initialize the
.IR area
with 
.IR zone [ size ]
as the memory space.
.P
The
.BR expr_area_wipe[_monotonic]()
wipe all allocated space of
.IR area ,
the
.BR expr_area_wipe_monotonic()
also resets the counter.
.P
The
.BR expr_area_reset_monotonic()
resets the counter without wiping the area.
.P
The
.BR expr_area_resize()
modifies the size of
.IR zone .
.P
The
.BR expr_area_malloc[3]()
allocate
.I size
bytes from
.IR zone .
.P
The
.BR expr_area_realloc[4]()
modify the size of
.I old
to
.I size
bytes the old data will be unchanged on expanding.
.P
The
.BR expr_area_dealloc()
releases the space of
.IR old .
.P
The
.BR expr_area_calloc()
is like
.B expr_area_malloc()
but always sets
.BR EXPR_AZERO .
.P
The
.BR expr_area_summary()
travels through all of
.I area
and write the summary to
.IR info .
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR expr_area_init[4]() , expr_area_resize() , expr_area_summary()
return 0 on success and negative value on fail.
.P
The
.BR expr_area_{m,re,c}alloc[3|4]()
return the pointer to the new space with
.IR size
and NULL on fail. The
.I old
will be unchanged if expr_area_realloc[4] fail.
.SH WARNING
The
.I old
for
.BR expr_area_dealloc()
cannot be
.BR NULL .
.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
T{
.na
.nh
.BR expr_area_*()
T}	Thread safety	MT-Safe
.TE
.SH HISTORY
.TP
.BR expr_area_*()
2026-10-06
.TQ
